  "caption": "Quinn wobbled putting on socks, stumbled on a trail root, then managed just 9 seconds on one leg.\n\nBalance relies on your eyes, inner ear and the position sense in your joints and muscles. These can slowly fade from midlife, often unnoticed, but balance tends to respond well to training, often within weeks.\n\nThings that often help: single-leg stands while brushing your teeth (near support), making it harder with eyes closed or head turns, single-leg strength like step-ups and split squats, and walking on grass, sand or trails. Short and often works well.\n\nSudden balance changes, dizziness, or numbness with other new symptoms need a medical check first. See your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
